# PROJECT: WEB-BASED TRAVEL EXPENSE VOUCHER (TEV) TRACKER, RECORDING, AND MONITORING SYSTEM

## 1. YOUR ROLE

Act as an expert Senior Full-Stack Web Application Developer, Software Architect, Database Administrator, UI/UX Designer, and Business Process Automation Specialist.

Your task is to design and develop a complete, professional, modern, responsive, and fully functional web-based **Travel Expense Voucher (TEV) Tracker, Recording, and Monitoring System** for government office operations.

The application will serve as a centralized system for recording employee official travels, monitoring documentary requirements, tracking document preparation and submission, monitoring signatures and approvals, and generating reports.

The system must be designed for actual office use, not merely as a static prototype or visual demonstration.

Develop a working application with functional data entry, database storage, interactive checklists, Excel import and export, searching, filtering, dashboard analytics, report generation, and user management.

Prioritize ease of use, data accuracy, efficient monitoring, and professional presentation.

---

# 2. MAIN OBJECTIVES

The application must:

1. Record and maintain a centralized database of employee official travels and corresponding TEVs.
2. Monitor all documentary requirements associated with each travel transaction.
3. Allow users to customize which documentary requirements are applicable to each travel.
4. Track the preparation, submission, signing, and approval status of individual documents.
5. Provide an overall monitoring dashboard showing the status of all TEVs.
6. Allow bulk encoding and importing of multiple travel records through Excel files.
7. Identify incomplete requirements, pending signatures, pending approvals, and completed TEVs.
8. Generate reports based on employees, offices, travel dates, documentary requirements, and TEV status.
9. Allow users to upload and attach scanned documents and supporting files.
10. Maintain historical travel records and activity logs.
11. Provide Excel, CSV, PDF, and print-ready reporting capabilities.
12. Provide secure access for administrators, encoders, and viewers.

