## MODULE 4: AUTOMATIC TEV STATUS AND COMPLIANCE MONITORING

Automatically calculate the overall status of each TEV based on its applicable documentary requirements.

Use the following classifications:

- NOT STARTED – No applicable requirement has been prepared.
- IN PROGRESS – At least one applicable requirement is being processed.
- FOR SUBMISSION – Prepared documents are awaiting submission.
- FOR SIGNATURE – Documents are awaiting signatures.
- FOR APPROVAL – Documents are awaiting approval.
- COMPLETED – All applicable requirements have been prepared, submitted, signed, and approved.
- ON HOLD – Manually placed on hold by an authorized user.

### A. Compliance Percentage

Calculate:

Compliance Percentage = (Number of Fully Approved Applicable Requirements / Total Applicable Requirements) × 100

Display the percentage using a progress bar.

Requirements marked Not Applicable must be excluded.

If no requirements are selected, display "No Requirements Selected."

### B. Important Status Rules

1. Each TEV must have its own independent checklist.
2. Only applicable requirements count toward compliance.
3. Prepared, Submitted, Signed, and Approved are separate stages.
4. All four stages must be completed before a requirement is considered fully completed.
5. A TEV is completed only when all applicable requirements are fully completed.
6. A manually assigned On Hold status must remain visible until an authorized user releases the hold.
7. All changes must automatically update dashboard statistics.
8. Do not allow contradictory status information.
9. Record the user and timestamp for every status change.

