# 6. CRITICAL SYSTEM-WIDE RULES

Follow these requirements strictly:

1. Each employee can have multiple TEV records.
2. Each TEV must have an independent documentary checklist.
3. Documentary requirements must be customizable per transaction.
4. Only applicable requirements count toward compliance.
5. Prepared, Submitted, Signed, and Approved are separate processing stages.
6. Approval must not automatically mean a document was signed.
7. All applicable documents must complete all four stages before the TEV is classified as Completed.
8. Updating one record must not affect other records.
9. Excel imports and manual encoding must use the same validation and database rules.
10. All imported records must appear immediately on the dashboard.
11. Dashboard statistics must reflect actual database records.
12. Dashboard filters must consistently update all associated charts, cards, and tables.
13. Deleting or modifying records must update dashboard statistics.
14. Historical travel records must preserve the office information applicable at the time of recording.
15. All important changes must be recorded in the Activity Logs.
16. Prevent duplicate reference numbers.
17. Do not automatically assume every documentary requirement is applicable to every travel.
18. Do not hardcode dashboard statistics.
19. Do not leave placeholder buttons or nonfunctional menu items.
20. Ensure data integrity during bulk Excel imports and updates.

